# Email Configuration for Report Sharing
# To enable actual email sending, configure these environment variables:

# Primary Configuration: Plesk SMTP (if properly configured)
EMAIL_HOST=mw265.com
EMAIL_PORT=587
EMAIL_USER=audit.report@mw265.com
EMAIL_PASS=Bd1ey413^

# Alternative Configurations (automatically tried by system):
# 1. Alternative Plesk SMTP with SSL (port 465)
# 2. Gmail SMTP (if Plesk mail is not working)

# Gmail Configuration (if needed as fallback)
# EMAIL_HOST=smtp.gmail.com
# EMAIL_PORT=587
# EMAIL_USER=your-gmail@gmail.com
# EMAIL_PASS=your-gmail-app-password

# Note: Based on Plesk mail settings:
# - If Plesk mail is "Not configured", email sending will fail
# - If "Disabled for incoming mail", only sending might work
# - If "Only using Sendmail", SMTP may not work
# 
# The system will automatically try multiple configurations:
# 1. Standard SMTP with STARTTLS (port 587)
# 2. Alternative SMTP with SSL (port 465) 
# 3. Gmail as fallback

# For Gmail, you need to:
# 1. Enable 2-factor authentication
# 2. Generate an App Password: https://myaccount.google.com/apppasswords
# 3. Use the App Password as EMAIL_PASS
